WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.594
The OWASP Top 10 provides a practical recap of common application risks: broken access control, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design, misconfiguration, vulnerable components, authentication failures, integrity failures, logging failures, and SSRF.

2
00:00:20.594 --> 00:00:35.420
PCI DSS responsibilities span secure development, secure configuration, vulnerability management, access control, authentication, cardholder data protection, logging, monitoring, and risk management.

3
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.733
Application teams contribute to many of those outcomes.

4
00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:51.514
Application security and payment protection are connected because payment systems depend on code, APIs, deployment pipelines, cloud services, identity systems, and operational processes.

5
00:00:51.514 --> 00:00:57.660
A secure payment application requires shared responsibility across technical and compliance teams.

6
00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.325
Completion of this course is awareness training.

7
00:01:00.325 --> 00:01:08.726
It does not constitute PCI DSS certification, assessment completion, or proof of full organizational compliance.

8
00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:14.423
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, PCI DSS v4.

9
00:01:14.423 --> 00:01:24.540
0 references, secure coding checklists, a payment application glossary, an OWASP-to-PCI mapping matrix, and a secure payment application checklist.

10
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.115
Use this course as a planning and awareness aid.

11
00:01:27.115 --> 00:01:33.511
Validate PCI DSS applicability with qualified assessment and internal compliance teams.

12
00:01:33.511 --> 00:01:39.408
Maintain evidence for secure development, testing, monitoring, and remediation activities.

